{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "Who else, besides yourself and your child, is typically involved in the outing, and what does each person contribute to the preparation or coordination?",
      "answer": "A partner is involved, confirming who will accompany the child and checking reusable items against the inventory. An accompanying caregiver may also join and is notified of any plan changes. A venue contact is referenced but their specific contribution to preparation is not specified beyond providing venue information."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "What specific items or information do you need to gather or confirm before you can leave the house — for example, packed bags, medications, snacks, or weather checks?",
      "answer": "You need to confirm the outing time and venue information, check attendee availability, and verify reusable items against a household inventory list. An outing checklist is prepared to guide packing. Specific item types such as medications or snacks are not specified in the workflow."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "What has to be true for you to decide the family is ready to go — is there a mental checklist, a confirmation from someone else, or another condition you verify before departing?",
      "answer": "Two conditions must be met: the venue plan is confirmed and the accompanying caregiver is confirmed, and all required items are available and packed. If either condition fails, you either contact the venue, rearrange the plan, find a substitute item, or postpone the outing."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "What do you do if something disrupts the plan at the last minute, such as another participant cancelling, an item being unavailable, or your child feeling unwell?",
      "answer": "You resolve missing items or change the outing plan, then notify accompanying caregivers of any changes. Recognised exceptions include venue plan changes, an accompanying caregiver becoming unavailable, and a required item being missing. The decision to change or postpone remains with the caregivers, not an automated system."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "How often does this outing routine happen — is it a daily, weekly, or occasional event, and does the process change depending on the type of outing?",
      "answer": "The routine occurs approximately once most weekends in this household. Whether the process changes depending on the type of outing is not specified in the workflow."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "When you 'put things away for next time,' what specifically does that involve — do you update any list, restock supplies, or note anything for future outings?",
      "answer": "After returning, you record which items were used and restock the bag. The household inventory list is updated accordingly. Automated restocking reminders can be generated from the recorded usage. Noting observations or plans for future outings beyond restocking is not specified."
    }
  ]
}
